    "q-73627": {
      "dom_id": "step-q73627",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14133484/assets/377a871e9328e0a8b3c12d8904ecc16a2e6e3a17fa7dba05925bb6f2e5d7e4ad.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=4$ and the vertical radius has length $b=6.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{6}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
